        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For a treadmill on a hard floor, buy a set of firm Sorbothane pads such
            as the Isolate It! 4 x 4-inch squares</strong>, identical under every foot, and level the
            machine after fitting them. If the treadmill is upstairs, put a thick dense rubber mat
            under it first; pads alone will soften the noise below, not remove it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, stability comes first: no stacking, no soft foam, no mismatched pads,
            and check them every few weeks. If the treadmill rocks or shakes even on a level floor,
